## Key Findings

### Salience Profile Impact

- Topic boosting produces measurable nDCG improvement for domain-specific queries
- PersonaContext self-reference provides bounded (±15%) but consistent re-ranking
- Personality modifiers affect valence/arousal encoding within safe [0.85, 1.15] bounds

### Retrieval Stack

- HYBRID (BM25 + Vector) provides best general-purpose quality
- VECTOR_ONLY works for purely semantic queries but misses keyword matches
- KEYWORD_ONLY handles exact-term queries (error codes, names) better

### Subsystem Contributions

- Graph augmentation (Hebbian, Entity, Temporal) provides incremental recall improvement
- Importance/decay scoring is the strongest contributor after vector similarity
- Tag gating provides near-zero-cost candidate elimination

